@startuml agent-run-git-deadline
' cumin works - every git command of the work directory ends after a
' deadline.
' Document: agent-run.md, topic on the work directory.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

rectangle "request the split,\nthe implementation, the review\n(internal/workflow)" as request
rectangle "cleanup of closed issues\n(internal/workflow)" as cleanup
rectangle "Workspace\ninternal/agent/worktree.go\nPrepare, Remove, Head, ..." as workspace
rectangle "git\n(clone, fetch, worktree, rev-parse, ...)" as git

request --> workspace
cleanup --> workspace
workspace -[#red,bold]-> git : <color:red>every git command ends\n<color:red>after 5 minutes</color>

note right of workspace
  A command that does not end
  is killed at the deadline.
  The error names the command and says
  that the deadline passed.
  The caller handles it
  as any failed git command.
end note

note right of git
  A child process of git
  can keep the output pipe open.
  2 seconds after the deadline,
  the pipe is closed
  and the command returns.
end note
@enduml
